  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "09-A",
      "x": 650,
      "y": 380,
      "bodyText": "Entry 104. I built the shadow dash into the light-constructs as an emergency measure. The ability to move through darkness for a single moment without being consumed by it. I built it and then forgot I built it. The wanderer has found it. They are going to need it.",
      "unlock": "SHADOW_DASH",
      "gate": ["DODGE", "WALL_CLING"]
    },
    {
      "id": "09-B",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 680,
      "bodyText": "Entry 112 — FINAL LOG BEFORE LOCK. I know what is coming. I know what the wanderer will try to do. I know that I will try to stop them, not because I want to but because I will not be able to help it. The corruption is in the cores and the cores are in me and I am in the apprentice and the window is the only thing still connecting this world to anything real. If the wanderer destroys the cores, the corruption ends. I end. If the wanderer fails, the simulation continues. I continue. I have written 112 log entries. Every single one was addressed to the apprentice. This one is addressed to the wanderer: I am sorry I was not still myself when you arrived. The light inside you was always supposed to lead you home.",
      "unlock": "NONE"
    }
  ],
